# CLOSING BLOCK [CLOSING]
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# --- X1: Policy ---
# scripture: Keep thy heart with all diligence — Proverbs 4:23
# never:
#   - Remove .env and secrets patterns without team discussion
#   - Remove 3-block documentation structure
#   - Remove Cv verification section
# careful:
#   - Removing patterns (may expose sensitive files)
#   - Broad patterns like * or **/* (may exclude needed files)
#   - Patterns affecting shared IDE configs
# safe:
#   - Add new pattern categories
#   - Add project-specific patterns
#   - Add comments explaining patterns
#   - Use ! to include specific files from ignored directories
#
# --- X4: Reference ---
# related_files:
#   - env.env — must be excluded by gitignore (co-located)
#   - editorconfig.editorconfig — co-located editor config
#   - gitmessage.gitmessage — co-located commit template
#   - template.mk — co-located build system template
# validate: git check-ignore -v [file]
# debug: cat .gitignore | grep -v '^#'
#
# --- X5: Note ---
# note:      Gitignore defines repository boundaries — what belongs in version
#            control and what should remain local or generated
# scripture: A time to keep, and a time to cast away — Ecclesiastes 3:6
# anchor:    Genesis 1:1 anchors everything
#
# --- X6: Template ---
# usage:     cp gitignore.gitignore .gitignore -> update pragma -> fill patterns
# update:
#   - Update M1 key and title for project
#   - Update M2 dates
#   - Add project-specific patterns to Co categories
#   - Update M5 cross_format references
# after:
#   - git check-ignore -v to verify patterns
#   - Remove X6 section
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# END CLOSING [END]
